          "enhanced_information": "Management for sickle cell disease should include penicillin prophylaxis until age 5 to prevent infections, in addition to increasing fiber in the diet and starting hydroxyurea. Iron supplementation is not typically recommended in sickle cell disease unless there is evidence of iron deficiency. Folate supplementation is important for patients with sickle cell disease, but it is typically started earlier than age 5. Ursodeoxycholic acid and vaccination for parvovirus are not standard components of sickle cell disease management."
